"The prognosis is influenced by several factors, including a preoperative PSA of 12.3 and positive surgical margins. The pathological findings show an ISUP grade group 2 (Gleason 3+4) with no extraprostatic extension and no seminal vesicle invasion. A key limitation is the absence of nodal sampling; therefore, pNx status cannot be definitively classified as pN0. Biopsy-to-prostatectomy comparison shows a slight difference in Gleason patterns noted between the initial biopsy (3+3) and the prostatectomy specimen (3+4). The lack of documented postoperative PSA or follow-up data significantly widens prognostic uncertainty regarding future trajectory. Information such as subsequent PSA levels and their pattern would be crucial for refining this assessment. The fixed estimated horizon is 56.82 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 34.09–79.54 months; its coverage has not been validated."
